From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 20:07:09 -0400
Subject: ui: a split's row parts end at their panes, the Space row shrinks
 before its dots, no folder count

The owner's notes of 2026-10-21 on 0.3.0 beta 1:

- A split's address row (toolbar T41): each pane's part ends at the pane's
  own edge, its top corners rounded as the card's, and the window's ground
  shows over the gap between the panes, as it does between the panes below.
  The parts had met in a soft blend over the gap, which read as a smudge
  where a dark page met a light one. The owner chose this over a sharp edge
  at the gap's middle from captures of both (splits J16).
- The Space row at the bottom of the sidebar (spaces B24): as the row
  narrows, after the gaps between the chips close, the row's leading inset,
  beside the downloads button, closes from 12 DIP to 4, and the chips and
  the "+" shrink a DIP at a time to 16 DIP, each glyph two thirds of its
  chip, before any chip turns to a dot. The trailing inset stays 10 DIP, so
  the "+" keeps as far from the sidebar's end as the downloads button keeps
  from its start. Eight Spaces keep their icons down to a row 190 DIP wide,
  where they had turned to dots below 272 with room left at the row's ends.
  As dots, the gaps close from 12 DIP down to 2 as the row narrows, so the
  "+" stays in the row; it had been pushed out of a narrow sidebar.
- A collapsed folder's header shows no count of its tabs (folders F33), as
  Arc's has none; the numbers read as noise beside the names.
- A capture parameter, split_tabs/1 on SteddingArcStyleWindow, puts a new
  window's first two tabs side by side, so a split's row can be captured
  without a drag (docs/HANDOFF.md, dev parameters).

Tests: SwitcherRulesTest (each step's form for eight Spaces, every width from
190 to 290 filled, the dots' gaps, the glyph size);
PageColourRowTest.ASplitRowTakesEachPanesColour reads the ground over the gap;
FolderViewTest.ACollapsedHeaderShowsNoNumber,
FolderRowsTest.ACollapsedFolderShowsNoNumberInAnySpace and
FolderTabsTest.ACollapsedFolderKeepsItsRows find the name alone on a
collapsed header.

Why: the owner found the blend ugly, the Space icons turning to dots with
room to spare, and the folder counts pointless.
Removable when: never; the next re-cut folds it into the patches that own
the split row, the Space row and the folder header.
